---
description: Bind this menu iteration's verified kitchen outputs to the resumable ledger checkpoint.
args:{ledger:KitchenLedger;checkpoint:KitchenCheckpoint;composition:{dishes:Dish[];sharedPrep:SharedPrep[];coverageGaps:string[]};tasting:{dishes:Dish[];sharedPrep:SharedPrep[];preferenceNotes:string[];repeatableDefects:string[];invalidatedDishIds:string[]};scaledBatches:ScaledBatch[];findings:MenuFinding[]}
returns:KitchenProposal
---
Build the chef packet from the post-tasting dishes and shared preparation, not the pre-tasting composition. Preserve the exact supplied scaled-batch artifact and all findings. Construct a new KitchenCheckpoint for this result: set ledgerRevision from the current ledger revision; list each current dish recipe revision and each current ingredient lot revision; include every prior invalidatedDishId plus each tasting invalidation, without duplication; retain checkpoint.costMinor because no exact cost artifact is provided by these arguments. A hard blocked ingredient, allergen, yield, cost, equipment or disclosure finding makes the proposal blocked; any review finding or repeatable tasting defect makes it review; otherwise it is ready-for-chef only when coverageGaps is empty. Carry subjective preference notes as chef-facing disclosures and never convert them alone into a block. Return the complete KitchenProposal with this updated checkpoint so the next kitchen iteration can resume from the reconciled state.
